==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Alternative forms===
* [[gobbledegook]]; [[gobblygook]], [[gobbly-gook]]

===Etymology===
First attested in a memo by US Representative (Texas) {{w|Maury Maverick}} dated March 30, 1944, banning "gobbledygook language"

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-gobbledygook.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|informal|lang=en}} [[nonsense|Nonsense]]; [[meaningless]] or [[encrypted]] language.
# {{context|informal|lang=en}}  Something written in an overly [[complex]], [[incoherent]], or [[incomprehensible]] manner.

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:nonsense]]

